(i) **Isotopes** are atoms of the same element (same atomic number, so the same number of protons) that have **different numbers of neutrons**, and therefore different mass numbers. Example: $^{35}_{17}\mathrm{Cl}$ and $^{37}_{17}\mathrm{Cl}$.

(ii) The atomic number of chlorine is **17** (the subscript in $^{37}_{17}\mathrm{Cl}$ and $^{35}_{17}\mathrm{Cl}$).

(iii) For Cl-37 (mass number 37, atomic number 17):

- **Protons = 17** (equal to the atomic number);
- **Neutrons = 37 - 17 = 20**;
- **Electrons = 17** (an atom is neutral, so electrons = protons).
